  "tldr": "A local exposure-IPW score on one buffered Følner interval splits exactly into assignment noise and a stationary Palm population score. The new kernel characterizes the disappearance of population uncertainty by the finite projection identity \\(\\Omega_{\\mathrm{pop}}=\\mathbb E_P[(\\sum_{k=-r}^{r}\\mathcal P_0h_k)^2]\\): zero variance is equivalent to a causal coboundary, not to homogeneous effects, and the vanished Gaussian coordinate is replaced by an endpoint-difference law at scale \\(N_n\\). A two-wave randomized diagnostic is left as the first-class open problem. The proposal uses no graph-distance quadratic, HAC premise, or alternating finite-volume regime.",
