  "related_work": "Leung2022ANI supplies the exposure-IPW score and fixed-population local-dependence perspective, but its target conditions on the realized graph and potential outcomes. ElMachkouriVolnyWu2013 supplies physical-dependence central limit tools for iid-innovation fields; the present finite-range model uses its settled short-range substrate rather than claiming a stronger field CLT. BaryshnikovYukich2005 and EichelsbacherRaicSchreiber2015 identify covariance limits and sufficient nondegeneracy mechanisms for stabilizing geometric functionals, respectively, but their Poisson geometric objects and variance criteria do not nest the causal projection frontier here. LiWager2022 studies direct and indirect effects under a generally dense graphon model and reports direct-effect Gaussian limits with conservative variance bounds; the present object is a sparse local exposure contrast and an exact zero-versus-positive Palm component. FanLengWu2025 studies regression adjustment and consistent variance estimation under its network-interference model; its estimand, graph model, and adjusted variance estimator differ from the two-wave Palm projection diagnostic. Leonov1961 is the probability-theory ancestor for the coboundary step, so the generic coboundary equivalence is treated as mathematical substrate rather than as a freestanding novelty claim.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The one-dimensional finite-range restriction is deliberate. It makes the innovation projection finite and the boundary loss exact, but it does not by itself cover approximate neighborhood interference, exponentially stabilizing random radii, graph-distance HAC, or higher-dimensional coboundary decompositions. The historical Bond et al. experiment cannot implement the proposed replicate diagnostic because it contains no second conditionally independent realization of the same potential-outcome experiment.",
  "honest_scope": "Theorem 1 is the exact causal projection frontier; Theorem 2 translates it into the alternate population-mean limit; Theorem 3 embeds both in the exposure-IPW limit. Leonov-type coboundary theory and stationary finite-dependent central limit theory are settled ingredients, while the feasible two-wave boundary diagnostic is open. As a cited sanity check, the homogeneous case \\(h_i=0\\) lies on the zero side, consistent with assignment-dominated direct-effect limits discussed by LiWager2022, but Proposition 2 shows that homogeneity is not necessary.",
